# Rust
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.orig
# cargo-fuzz
**/fuzz/target
**/fuzz/corpus
**/fuzz/artifacts

# PHP (narrowed to php/** so the repo-root `vendor/` — the M1 tokio-postgres fork — is NOT
# ignored; see M1-S1 task 1)
php/**/vendor
**/.phpunit.cache
**/.phpunit.result.cache
**/composer.lock.orig

# Bench outputs are COMMITTED (bench/results/*.json) per SPEC §16 — do not ignore them.

# M1-S8b: testkit/dbal-suite.sh's work directory — a PINNED git clone of doctrine/dbal plus its
# vendor/ and the generated phpunit config. Never commit a vendored clone; the tag in the runner is
# the single source of truth for which suite the recorded numbers came from.
/.dbal-suite

# M1-S9: testkit/orm-suite.sh's work directory — a PINNED git clone of doctrine/orm plus its
# vendor/, the generated phpunit configs, the junit logs and the run's ferrod log. Same rule as
# .dbal-suite: never commit a vendored clone; the tag in the runner is the single source of truth
# for which suite the recorded numbers came from.
/.orm-suite

# M1-S8c: testkit/migrations-e2e.sh's harness. `composer.lock` IS committed — it is what pins
# doctrine/migrations for a reproducible run. Its vendor tree, the migration classes
# `migrations:diff` regenerates on every run, and the run's ferrod log are not.
testkit/migrations/vendor
testkit/migrations/generated
testkit/migrations/ferrod.log

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local env / secrets (DSNs live in ferrod config, never committed)
.env
*.local.toml
